# expect-error: returns a closure of a different signature
# A [Proc …]-returning proc that returns a closure VALUE verbatim whose signature
# does NOT match the declared return is rejected. Here the param is
# [Proc [i32] i32] but the declared return is [Proc [f32] f32]. (A conforming
# return, or an inline-literal tail that monomorphizes, is accepted.)
proc bad {[Proc [i32] i32] f} [Proc [f32] f32] { $f }
proc main {} { print "x" }
main
